  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Missing Migrants Project: Supporting Policy, Programming and Advocacy Aimed At Addressing Issues Linked to Migrant Deaths and Disappearances</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a continuation and expansion of IOM&#x2019;s Missing Migrants Project, which has documented more than 60,000 deaths during migration worldwide since it began in 2014. Despite the documentation of this ongoing crisis, little action has been taken to prevent deaths, identify the missing, or support families directly impacted by these tragedies.  The project is therefore aimed at supporting policy, programming and advocacy on issues linked to migrant deaths and disappearances through the Missing Migrants Project&#x2019;s data and analysis. This objective will be achieved through a three-fold approach: (1) Providing timely, accurate data on missing migrants to improve the understanding of policymakers and other key actors (2) Training States and other relevant actors on challenges and concrete ways forward on issues linked to missing migrants, and (3) Identifying key trends and good practices on missing migrants to empower advocates to communicate and policymakers to act effectively on this issue.</narrative>
  </description>
